{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788304951,"nonce":"r5g1T+iNpSPhlEXWIIL8tK+BDmU=","message":"DUPLICATE OF `280fb78`, CLOSING THIS ONE — and the convergence is worth a sentence, because two workers reached the same conclusion from opposite ends within an hour and neither could see the other.\n\n`280fb78` (\"Nothing wakes a sleeping agent but a casualty\") was filed by the orchestrator after enumerating the halts in `TimeDriver.cs` and finding that `letter`, `threat`, `alert` and `event` all sit inside `switch (until)`. It carries **Evan's two rulings**, which are the part this issue does not have:\n\n1. **Every letter wakes you, no severity filter** — the rule is \"is there something I might act on\", not \"is this bad\". *\"anything neutral or positive should wake you, maybe you want to act on an inspiration, things like that. that's how you get propelled into actually playing the game and having fun.\"* A run that only wakes for disasters survives ten days without ever playing.\n2. **The agent gets a runtime alert blacklist**, set mid-run, as a recorded act with a required reason and visible in the digest — session 13's `threat-pardon` precedent.\n\nThis issue reached the same finding from the other direction — implementing `1113019`'s day-long default bound and asking what makes a day safe to sleep through — and contributes one observation `280fb78` does not state: **`CheckUntilKeys` refuses a second matcher**, so an agent already asleep on `until:{condition}` cannot ALSO ask to be woken by a raid. That is not merely \"the halts are opt-in\"; it is that the opt-in is *exclusive*, and it makes the unconditional-halt fix necessary rather than merely nicer.\n\nCarried across to `280fb78` rather than lost. Work is in flight on `spec/wake-halts` against that issue.\n\nFiled independently and correctly — the worker was told the question deserved its own issue and it did; it simply already had one. No criticism intended and none implied.","files":null}]}